# CMU 11-785 Cursor Maintenance Rules

## Content Edits
- When updating deadlines, lectures, staff, or syllabus, edit ONLY the YAML and Markdown files inside `content/semesters/<SEMESTER>/`.
- Do not edit raw HTML files or generated tables directly.
- Ensure all dates conform to ISO-8601 strings (e.g. `2026-09-18T23:59:00-04:00`).
- Ensure all URLs are syntactically valid and absolute.

## Design & UI Edits
- Refer to `DESIGN.md` for all color tokens and typography rules.
- Maintain CMU Tartan Red (`#A80000`) as primary brand accent.
- Adhere to WCAG 2.2 Level AA accessibility: use semantic `<nav>`, `<button>`, and `<a href="...">` elements. Never use clickable `<span>` elements for links.
- Use CSS Custom Properties defined in `DESIGN.md`.

## Safety Constraints
- NEVER run `git push` or modify remote repositories. Keep all changes local.
- NEVER delete or overwrite existing educational binary assets (PDFs, PPTXs, IPYNBs, ZIPs).
- Always verify changes locally using `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm build`.
